  "prefLabel": "En 402.04 Competitive local exchange carrier (CLEC)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 402.04 “Competitive local exchange carrier (CLEC)” means a carrier, and its successors and assigns, authorized by the commission after July 23, 1995 to provide telephone service for the public in a particular area within New Hampshire.\n\nSource. #14015, eff 7-1-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 400)",
